Z||000003||West Coast Fiero||12-03-2001||02:48 AM||||too much!!!!<P> this is Chris West's car ( owner of West Coast Fiero ) he has been tweaking the car since he bought it of the showroom floor in 1986<P>his first mod was a turbo 2.8 2 weeks after he bought the car, the 2.8 lasted about 2 months with 14lbs of boost =-)<P>second engine was a naturally aspirated 3.4 DOHC, I believe he was in the low 13's<P> now with the 3.4 DOHC, T3/T4 ceramic ball bearing water cooled turbo, linear curcuit for fual managment ( made here at West Coast Fiero - was one of the prototypes), headers, custom intake, fuel cooled injection for turbo set up, coil overs, delrin buching, custom made tubular a-arm, wildly custom interior, custom paint - inside and out...... I think over the 14 years he has had the car and with what is presently in it, including labor and parts, matbe in the range of 40k<P><P>------------------<BR>Technician, West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
