Z||000009||rogergarrison||12-03-2001||06:12 AM||||I dont run that much boost. My takeoff isnt that spectacular, but screams when its wound up. Supercharging is way to go for drag racing, you have max boost imediatlely. Personaly, Im not into drag racing, rather just drive fast on a twisty road. Going in a straight line for a block is not high on my list of fun things. (IMHO)||||reg||1
Z||000010||fieroX||12-03-2001||12:22 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by West Coast Fiero:<BR><B><P>last run in 1999 at Los Angeles County Race way - 11.98 at 139.4 mph<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>That is alot of mph for an 11.98.  I ran a program that tells me the average time for a 139.4 mph pass is 9.78.  That thing must have some massive wheelspin.  And 634 horsepower at the wheels. (758 at the crank)<BR>Sorry to be a sceptic.<BR><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fierox.com/logo2small.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Eric||12-03-2001||12:34 PM||||That claim is pretty far out, Eric.  If you wouldn't mind scanning a timeslip for us, you'll find that you may have more converts than doubters.  Also a picture of the Fiero in question passing through the traps after completing the run with the big board that shows your times in full view would help too.  I hope someone has a quarter mile to horsepower calculator.  That speed paired with that time tells me your boss did a massive burnout when the tree turned green.  Mid 9s should be possible with that kind of power on some drag slicks.  My guess is that 3.4 is pumping out close to 1000 (self destructing) horsepower.  I can only imagine how twisted up that Fiero's frame is now.<P>In the future, please be ready to back up your unbelievable claims with some hard evidence.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Eric||12-03-2001||12:38 PM||||Looks like Fiero x picked up the ball.  I had to relieve myself halfway through typing my post.  Just wish we could flush the rest of this crap off the forum too.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Turbo88||12-03-2001||12:45 PM||||You can have some outragous MPH with slow (comparitively) ets. One of the guys in the local F-Body club ran his Mecham Trans-Am last weekend to the tune of 15.08 at 124mph. It's amasing what a supercharged LS1 will do when you rev the hell out of it and dump the clutch on rock hard Goodyear RSAs. However high 11s at almost 140 in a fiero (where wheel spin on a high rpm band motor shouldn't be too bad) sounds up there. I wouldn't mind seeing the timeslip. Not to be totally skeptic but I would love to see the other stats like RT, 60' 660mph 990et/mph ect. As soon as my house is done, I believe I am going to drop the 2.8 pushrod turbo motor and try the TDC setup with a hybrid. <P>Give us some details on that car, I'm curious about the ECM-AFC integration and what other motor mods he made. The TDC/DOHC are all forged bottomends if I recall which makes them a prime candidate for a power adder. Though compression is a bit high..||||reg||1
Z||000014||Formula88||12-03-2001||12:47 PM||||WOW!  I'm not doubting the times.  Very possible considering that car is basically a rolling ad for West Coast Fiero.  Makes the 3.4DOHC look even better.  I can add the engine and enjoy good power and the sound right away, then maybe add a turbo later on!  Not looking for anything THAT wild, but I would like to be in the 12s or low 13s.  Basically, I don't want to have to worry about any newer Vette or F-body I might run into (unless it's modded, then all bets are off).  ||||reg||1
Z||000015||Formula88||12-03-2001||12:50 PM||||BTW, Tina's 383 V8 Fiero has run 11.98 (if memory serves), and a turbo 3.4 could easily be putting out similar horsepower.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Slammed Fiero||12-03-2001||01:14 PM||||How easily you all get off track.<P>She asked for a turbo , I assume on a 2.8 which is what she has...not a DOHC.<P>mid to low 14's I would say and still be reliable. I say reliable because her motor has 80,000 miles plus on it and insane boost levels are probably not wise. <P>The Fiero shops car was running high 13's with an intercooler. But this is a little more elaborate setup with a Turbonetics Delta Gat and a blow off valve. and 12lbs boost(?)<P>Fiero X is dead on ..the speed is kinda <BR>outrageous for the time. I think your caught in a lie. By comparison I have seen 10 sec supras run mid 130's in the 1/4 your running right ont he barrie at a 11.98 but your 9 mph faster?? Atleast research your fairy tales.<P><BR>"Chris used the 92 DOHC computer with his own fuel management system "<P>In the picture it looked identical to the electromotive system I just got..Hmmmmmm.<BR>yeah a Turbo Fiero can be made to be fast , but a v8 will do it a lot cheaper and with a lot less stress / effort...<P>It's called Torque.<P>As for your turbo Lisa. Just run 5-6 Lbs of boost unless you are planning to rebuild the motor. Later you can add an inercooler and all sorts of stuff. Just like building a house make sure the foundation is good before you go adding to it.<P>For the money you may be better off to drop in a 3.4 then plan a turbo later on. That way you get a fresh motor which is good to build on.<P>JM <P>------------------<BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, Big Bore TB, 70Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
Z||000017||Borgio||12-03-2001||03:00 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B><BR>In the picture it looked identical to the electromotive system I just got..Hmmmmmm.<BR>yeah a Turbo Fiero can be made to be fast , but a v8 will do it a lot cheaper and with a lot less stress / effort...<P>It's called Torque.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>What do you mean? Turbos have sufficient torque. Its not the engine speed that gives you so much power, as said in another post its basically artificial displacement.<P>Also maybe the 1/4 speed was just a typo. Don't be so hard on him and assume he was lying.||||reg||1
Z||000018||Slammed Fiero||12-03-2001||04:34 PM||||No he has been saying 11.99's for a while , this is the first time I have seen him post the trap speed.<P>I had a merkur with 18 Psi of Boost , it went like hell once you had it going , but off the line it was a dead mule.<P>Import turbo racers use a progressive NOS system on the more elaborate Turbo cars to make up for the lack of low end grunt. (get them outta the hole) <P><BR>As for peoples claims , on this forum you will quickly find out not everything you read is true.<P>Anyone remeber the guy with a turbo N* who ran low 12's?? when we asked Dennis at design one who supposedly built the car he had never even heard of it.<P>Unfortunatley there is fortune is publishing misinformation. <P>JM ||||reg||1
