Z||000032||sluppy123||12-04-2001||11:10 PM||||No time slip but G-tech says it will do the 1/4 in 14.3 . Engine is an internally stock 2.8 bored .03 over, ported intake, heads and exhaust, compu-cam. Auto trans with B&M shift kit.<P>------------------<BR>-Brian, Toolmaker<BR>Lincoln, NE<BR>87' GT- Turbo Charged, Modified 2.8- 235 HP w/ 7 psi Boost,<BR>                 <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1711832&a=12781563&p=54316496&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||1
Z||000033||Eric||12-05-2001||02:51 AM||||I hate being right.<P>Lisa, why don't you just look at Roger's setup?  It's mostly stock, except for the bottom end.  Not a lot of money in it either.  I was seriously considering fabbing up my own turbo on a shoestring.  So if cost is the main point to your argument, I think turbos can be an economical solution to an air-starved engine.  2.8s should make it down the track around 14 seconds in the mid to high 90 mph range (or for those of us on the left coast, 125mph+).  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000034||Mach10||12-05-2001||04:51 AM||||ROFL... Supras with EXCELLENT traction at 800hp?!?? You should see the ones on the street in my area... Sorry, but NO. They turn WICKED times, and look like a stage-rocket the whole way down the track...||||reg||10
Z||000035||lou_dias||12-05-2001||09:13 AM||||I've checked out one of the supra forums and they do pull 13's with very high trap speeds.<P>With big turbos, it takes longer to spool up but when it does, watch out.  So they limp off the line or they do too long a burnout.<BR>It's the norm when all your power comes from a turbo.  i don't doubt CFW's stats there.<BR>In a longer race you'd really see them shine.||||reg||1
Z||000036||fieroX||12-05-2001||11:44 AM||||I wont believe it until I see it.  I have seen thousands of passes at dragstrips all over the country.  I know how time coorelates to speed (to an extent) but that claim is ludicris.  Show a website where people are running 11's at 140 consistently.  I dont care what kind of car it is, but I guarantee you 99% of the cars in the high 11's will be running 116-124 mph range.  Prove it to me.||||reg||1
